@@ -8,5 +8,6 @@ GNU make 4.4.1 is built into `~/vlckit-build/tools` and passed as `VLC_PATH` (Vi
 `0018-avcodec-audio-coalesce-TrueHD-MLP-frames.patch` (pass 1d, D015) is a libvlc patch in VLCKit's own patch format: `build.sh` copies it into `libvlc/patches/` so VideoLAN's script applies it after the seventeen upstream ones. It makes the avcodec audio decoder gather the 40-sample TrueHD/MLP frames into ~20 ms blocks before the audio output; no other codec is touched.
 `0019-videotoolbox-dpb-no-latency-bump-ahead-of-arriving-picture.diff` (pass 1e, D017) is a libvlc patch in `git format-patch` form, stored as `.diff`; `build.sh` copies it into `libvlc/patches/` as `0019-….patch` so it is applied after 0018. In VideoToolbox's picture reorder buffer (`modules/codec/videotoolbox/dpb.c`), a release triggered only by the max-latency count no longer outputs pictures that follow the arriving picture in display order; VLC's own `dpb_test.c` "Max latency requirements" expectation, which encoded the out-of-order release, now expects display order. It affects HEVC and H.264 (the same reorder code), nothing else.
 `0020-es_out-forward-next-frame-need-data-only-from-stepped-es.diff` (pass 1i; no decision yet — pass 1i stopped at step 8) is a libvlc patch in the same form and install path as 0019 (copied into `libvlc/patches/` as `0020-….patch`, applied after 0019). In `src/input/es_out.c`, while VLC is frame stepping, only the stepped video ES's "need data" request reaches the input, and a request already standing is cleared when stepping starts. Without it a subtitle decoder's unmeetable request kept the demuxer reading while paused after a previous-frame step, and Play then started with the whole pause's worth of late pictures. Two lines, one file; paused seeks outside frame stepping are unchanged.
+`0021-es_out-no-late-pcr-compensation-while-paused.diff` (pass 2f) is a libvlc patch in the same form and install path as 0019 and 0020 (copied into `libvlc/patches/` as `0021-….patch`, applied after 0020). In `src/input/es_out.c`, a PCR that arrives while es_out is paused no longer goes through the late-PCR compensation, the same skip already made while frame stepping. Without it, a seek while paused is anchored at the pause date, the next PCR looks late by the time since the pause, and VLC flushes and rebuffers lap after lap without moving the demuxer, so the picture runs ahead of the seek target and Play starts from the read-ahead (pass 2e). One condition, one line.
 `build.sh` sets `TVOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 26.0` in VLCKit's own `VLCKit.xcodeproj` before building (pass 1e rerun 3, D018): Xcode 27 rejects tvOS deployment targets below 15.0 and the project ships 11.0, which VideoLAN's archive call does not override; libvlc's own minimum is unchanged.
 `PACKAGE_ONLY=1 tools/vlckit-truehd/build.sh` (pass 1e rerun 4, D018) packages the libvlc slices a previous full run left in `~/vlckit-build` — no clone, no patching, no host tools, no contrib or libvlc compile (VideoLAN's script with `-n -l`); step 2d (tvOS target 26.0) still runs, then the `nm` check and the copy to `Frameworks/`. Without it, the recipe is the full build as before.
